@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN. P17-ASSEMBLY-001's
rem and P17-SOLVE-001's copies each carried bare OLD_END lines -- leaked
rem heredoc terminators -- which cmd.exe reported into their .err files.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-VIZ-001 THE LOAD AND RESTRAINT GLYPHS (ADR-045). The exact
rem invocation, recorded so the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, TWENTY-FIVE in a row counting this one.
rem verify-harness.cmd beside it is its regression and was not edited.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem                        sha1sum         244b38de8feac0475af7cdc56ba9415d27d8dd29
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem                        sha1sum         afd0197d4f4726db7f533c2f27f4f6e069ba83c6
rem
rem BOTH FORMS ARE RECORDED because they differ and a hash without its
rem algorithm cannot be checked: .gitattributes sets `*.cmd text eol=crlf`, so
rem git stores LF while the working tree is CRLF. A note carrying only the
rem git-blob value makes a sha1sum check fail against a harness that is
rem correct, and this milestone lost ten minutes to exactly that.
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: this machine has 16 logical cores, so `cmake --build` lets Ninja
rem run 18 compiles at once, and a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy
rem translation units exhausted the commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens
rem nothing: the same sources, the same flags, -Werror included; the no-op
rem rebuild check still proves the binaries are the ones just built; the full
rem suite still runs unfiltered in all three presets. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT CHANGED SINCE ec68076, AND WHAT IS OWED BY IT.
rem
rem   NEW          include/bettercad/renderer/StructuralOverlay.hpp
rem                src/renderer/StructuralOverlay.cpp
rem                               The drawable geometry of the overlays, in SI
rem                               METRES. Every position comes from
rem                               Mesh::findNode -- the glyph structures carry
rem                               NO position, so the drawing layer resolves
rem                               them, and ADR-045 puts that resolution in the
rem                               headless layer because it is the part most
rem                               likely to be wrong.
rem                src/renderer/occt/OcctOverlayPresentation.hpp
rem                src/renderer/occt/OcctOverlayPresentation.cpp
rem                               Segments only, one colour per role, and
rem                               ComputeSelection DELIBERATELY EMPTY so an
rem                               annotation never comes between the user and
rem                               the element they clicked.
rem
rem   MODIFIED     include/bettercad/renderer/Viewer.hpp
rem                src/renderer/occt/OcctViewer.cpp
rem                               A QUALIFIED P16 FILE, for the third time in
rem                               this milestone. PresentationKind::Overlay and
rem                               Viewer::displayOverlay. Named `Overlay`
rem                               rather than `StructuralOverlay` so the KIND
rem                               and the struct it depicts do not share a
rem                               name.
rem                include/bettercad/renderer/StructuralInspection.hpp
rem                src/renderer/StructuralInspection.cpp
rem                               THE DEFECT FIX. inspectNode now takes the
rem                               MeshDofMap. See the next block.
rem                src/renderer/CMakeLists.txt
rem                               two sources registered.
rem                tests/renderer/StructuralResultViewTests.cpp
rem                               47 -> 66 cases, of which FOURTEEN need a GPU
rem                               and are tagged [frame]. Counted by parsing
rem                               the TEST_CASE declarations, not estimated.
rem
rem A DEFECT WAS FOUND IN COMMITTED, QUALIFIED CODE ON THE WAY IN, and it is
rem why StructuralInspection changed at all. inspectNode's comment said "every
rem restraint that names this node" and the loop unioned EVERY resolution's
rem mask, because RestraintResolution carries a mask and a node COUNT but
rem never a node list -- so it could not tell which restraints named the node
rem in hand. With a fixed support and a Uz-only support in one analysis, every
rem restrained node reported FIXED, and a UI drawing a support symbol from it
rem drew the wrong support. A fixture whose two restraints have DIFFERENT
rem masks is the only thing that can see it, which is why the first round of
rem tests missed it. See DEFECT_RESTRAINT_COMPONENTS.md.
rem
rem AND THE PROBES RAN BEFORE THIS RUN, not after it. Two batches:
rem
rem   batch 1   the glyph overlays        21 probes
rem             17 killed, 3 SURVIVED, 1 VOID
rem   batch 2   the gaps found by READING  7 probes
rem             7 killed, including re-runs of both real survivors
rem   P5        the last unprobed new test 1 probe
rem
rem   29 probe runs, 27 distinct mutations, 24 killed, 1 equivalent mutant
rem   (G20, documented), 1 void and superseded (G11), SIX real test gaps
rem   closed. See MUTATION_GLYPHS.md.
rem
rem THE TWO METHODS FOUND DISJOINT SETS, and that is the argument for doing
rem both: six gaps came from READING the pristine sources while batch 1 was
rem rewriting the working copies, and NOT ONE of them was a mutation batch 1
rem contained. Two more came from batch 1's survivors. Four of the six are
rem guards that were written, documented and never reached, because the only
rem callers in the tests produced correct input by construction.
rem
rem ONE SURVIVOR IS KEPT AS AN EQUIVALENT MUTANT RATHER THAN TESTED. G20 makes
rem the overlay selectable, but ComputeSelection is empty, so in either mode
rem the presentation owns no sensitive entity and nothing observable differs.
rem Writing a test would mean populating ComputeSelection to make a probe
rem fail -- changing production code to serve a test.
rem
rem THE MEASUREMENT THIS RUN PROTECTS. The arrows reach the screen at the
rem mesh's own scale, measured with the CAMERA HELD STILL because fitAll
rem reframes: display both, fitAll once, then hide the overlay with
rem setVisible, which does not move the camera. 36586 px with the overlay,
rem 36308 without, so the arrows contribute 278. The first version of that
rem assertion demanded that mesh-plus-overlay cover MORE pixels and measured
rem 42036 -> 36586 -- coverage went DOWN, because fitAll zooms out and the
rem mesh's silhouette shrinks faster than thin segments add pixels. The arrows
rem were correct and the assertion was not.
rem
rem THE ELEMENT CONTOURS ARE STILL NOT IN THIS RUN, because they are blocked
rem rather than unfinished. A boundary view names TRIANGLE ids and an element
rem channel is per TETRAHEDRON; meshing::Triangle carries no owning
rem tetrahedron and no accessor answers for one. Closing it needs a new
rem capability in the qualified P16 meshing module, which is a scope decision.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED from the
rem display run: `unit\.Structural` already covers unit.StructuralViz as a
rem substring, `unit\.View` covers Viewer, `unit\.Mesh` covers MeshView and
rem MeshDofMap, `architecture` covers the renderer-to-structural edge, and
rem `gui\.` covers the application that links the renderer. The glyph work
rem added no test outside unit.StructuralViz, so no new term is needed. The
rem SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS RUN rather than predicted here -- a
rem figure nobody has measured does not belong in the evidence for a run.
rem
rem NOT in the set: unit\.Unit and unit\.Quantity (no unit-system change),
rem unit\.Material and unit\.Mass (no material code changed), and the drawing
rem and assembly view tests, which link the renderer but were not touched by
rem it -- a link-order or symbol problem there is caught by the UNFILTERED run
rem in all three presets, which is where a change nobody predicted shows up.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem twelve milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating
rem one measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still
rem run UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
